{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## |''^### |revision r3|Revision r3|r3 reconciliation|Reconciliation'\"' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md\"","aggregated_output":"3:Status: design, proposed (2026-09-24, revision r3). Supersedes the\n10:revision r3 reconciles the round-2 consensus review by `gpt-6-sol`\n33:## 1. Objective and architectural position\n83:### 1.1 What this document adds over B6\n116:### 1.2 What this document does not add\n129:## 2. Governing invariants\n183:## 3. Identities: three kinds, one address space\n243:## 4. The fetch pipeline\n245:### 4.1 The format record\n290:### 4.2 The six steps\n424:### 4.3 Refusal vocabulary\n479:## 5. Format records for the four backends\n485:### 5.1 `:yin.ast/code` (the AST walker)\n517:### 5.2 `:yin.semantic/code` (the semantic VM)\n543:### 5.3 `:yin.debruijn.code` (the stack VM)\n565:### 5.4 `:yin.debruijn.register` (the register VM)\n585:### 5.5 Same-root pairing becomes derivation verification\n596:## 6. Linking is a stream exchange\n598:### 6.1 The topology\n648:### 6.2 Linker-local state\n670:### 6.3 The stepped interface\n734:### 6.4 `fetch` is host policy over an explicit runtime\n764:## 7. `(require 'foo)` lowers to the linker\n766:### 7.1 Today\n779:### 7.2 The unified flow\n909:### 7.3 Installing a module is a scheduler child task\n1004:### 7.4 Transitive requires and cycles\n1025:## 8. The manifest registry\n1027:### 8.1 The module manifest\n1119:### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n1184:### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\n1252:## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n1344:## 10. File box\n1382:## 11. Completion criteria\n1443:## 12. Open decisions\n1484:## 13. Reconciliation record\n1486:### 13.1 Revision r3 (round 2, `gpt-6-sol`)\n1545:### 13.2 Revision r2 (round 1, `gpt-5.6-sol`)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
