{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '243,478p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 243\"","aggregated_output":"   243\t## 4. The fetch pipeline\n   244\t\n   245\t### 4.1 The format record\n   246\t\n   247\tA format record is a plain map held in linker-local state. B6 fixed three\n   248\tfunction slots; this revision replaces one, renames one, and adds three:\n   249\t\n   250\t```clojure\n   251\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code      ; the dispatch key\n   252\t :contract            \"b1\"                    ; contract revision name\n   253\t :identity-fn         (fn [value] identity)   ; mint: publish! only\n   254\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [identity value] boolean) ; step 3\n   255\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 2, per part\n   256\t :validate-fn         (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 4, whole\n   257\t :obligations-fn      (fn [value] [sym ...])        ; step 5a: free names\n   258\t :definitions-fn      (fn [value] #{sym ...})       ; step 5a: own defs\n   259\t :parts-fn            (fn [value] [address ...])}   ; step 2 worklist\n   260\t```\n   261\t\n   262\t- `:identity-fn` mints an identity from a payload. It is used by\n   263\t  `publish!` and never by verification.\n   264\t- `:identity-matches-fn` is the step-3 check, directed by the identity.\n   265\t  For H and R it is `(= identity (image-hash value))`, a contract-pinned\n   266\t  hash with one algorithm. For the storage-derived formats it is\n   267\t  `(jing/segment-matches? identity value)`, so a value minted under\n   268\t  `:sha256` while the default is `:blake3` verifies under the algorithm\n   269\t  the identity names and never fails spuriously.\n   270\t- `:row-defect-fn` validates one fetched part on its own, before any\n   271\t  address it references is enqueued: tag, arity, slot kinds, saturation.\n   272\t  For single-payload formats it is the whole validator, run early.\n   273\t- `:parts-fn` returns the storage addresses a fetched payload references\n   274\t  and without which it is incomplete. For the three single-payload\n   275\t  formats it returns nothing. For `:yin.ast/code` it returns the child\n   276\t  row ids of a row body.\n   277\t- `:obligations-fn` returns the free names of a value.\n   278\t  `:definitions-fn` returns the constant store keys the value itself\n   279\t  binds at module level. The linker subtracts the second from the first\n   280\t  and joins the remainder with the manifest's declarations to form\n   281\t  obligations (step 5a). For the AST record both are Datalog over the\n   282\t  rows (`yin.vm/free-names` and the store-key query behind\n   283\t  `yin.vm/ast-requirements`); for the vector formats both are operand\n   284\t  scans (`:var` against `:store-put`, `:load-free` against the\n   285\t  `yin/def` call sites).\n   286\t\n   287\t`fetch` and `step` contain no branch on `:format`. Adding a fifth backend\n   288\tis one more record.\n   289\t\n   290\t### 4.2 The six steps\n   291\t\n   292\tThe order is B6's, unchanged, and remains load-bearing for the reasons\n   293\tB6 gives. An admission check precedes step 1; step 2 is a bounded\n   294\tworklist; steps 1 and 2 are stream exchanges (section 6); step 5 has a\n   295\tlinker half and a receiver half.\n   296\t\n   297\t```text\n   298\t(link runtime format identity)\n   299\t\n   300\t0. admission     request malformed                  -> :invalid-request\n   301\t                 no format record for the format    -> :unsupported-format\n   302\t                 request contract differs from the record's\n   303\t                                                    -> :contract-mismatch\n   304\t1. address    <- (index identity)               linker-local index\n   305\t                 absent entry                       -> :absent\n   306\t2. payload    <- fetch address over dao.stream\n   307\t                 absent payload                     -> :absent\n   308\t                 (not (segment-matches? address v)) -> :address-mismatch\n   309\t                 ((:row-defect-fn format) v)        -> :descriptor-defect\n   310\t                 bounds exceeded                    -> :parts-limit\n   311\t                 enqueue ((:parts-fn format) v); repeat until empty\n   312\t3.               (not ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity root))\n   313\t                                                    -> :hash-mismatch\n   314\t4.               ((:validate-fn format) whole) returns a defect\n   315\t                                                    -> :descriptor-defect\n   316\t5a.              obligations <- join free names with declarations\n   317\t                 free name with no declaration      -> :undeclared-free\n   318\t5b.  (receiver)  each obligation discharged by exact equality\n   319\t                 profile or manifest differs        -> :unresolved-free\n   320\t                 name bound in free env or store    -> :shadowed-free\n   321\t6. return the verified image as data\n   322\t```\n   323\t\n   324\tStep by step, for all four formats:\n   325\t\n   326\t0. **Admit the request.** Before any lookup or fetch, the linker checks\n   327\t   the request's shape against the closed key set of section 6.3\n   328\t   (`:invalid-request`), that it holds a format record for the requested\n   329\t   format (`:unsupported-format`), and that the request's\n   330\t   `:yin.link/contract`, when present, equals the record's `:contract`\n   331\t   (`:contract-mismatch`). The contract check runs here, ahead of step\n   332\t   2's row-local grammar check, so no validator ever runs under the\n   333\t   wrong table; revision r2 placed it in step 4, after row-local\n   334\t   validation had already run, which was an ordering defect. For a\n   335\t   manifest-delivered image the same check runs again against\n   336\t   `:yin.module/contract` immediately after the manifest is verified\n   337\t   and before any derivation or image is fetched (section 8.1).\n   338\t1. **Resolve identity to storage address.** The index is linker-local\n   339\t   composition data: a map, or datoms `[identity attribute address]`\n   340\t   read through `index-from-datoms` from a `dao.space` source the linker\n   341\t   observes with its own cursor. An entry that has not been observed\n   342\t   yet is `:absent` now, which is the honest answer at this moment; a\n   343\t   later request may find it. Step 1 never waits and never queries a\n   344\t   remote index inline. For the storage-derived formats the identity is\n   345\t   its own address and the index is the identity function.\n   346\t2. **Fetch payload over `dao.stream`.** Each address is a\n   347\t   `:jing/get-content` request on the content request stream and a\n   348\t   correlated response on the content response stream (section 6). The\n   349\t   value is verified against the address it was requested at, using the\n   350\t   algorithm the address carries (`jing/segment-matches?`). Then, before\n   351\t   any child is enqueued, `:row-defect-fn` validates this part alone;\n   352\t   a malformed row is refused here and its slots are never followed.\n   353\t   Then `:parts-fn` names further addresses; each is fetched and\n   354\t   verified the same way; the worklist is breadth-first from the root\n   355\t   and visits each address once. The composition supplies bounds in the\n   356\t   runtime: `:max-parts`, `:max-depth`, `:max-bytes`; exceeding any is\n   357\t   `:parts-limit` naming the bound and the address at which it was hit.\n   358\t   The result of step 2 is the root value plus, for a multi-part\n   359\t   format, the map of every fetched part by address.\n   360\t3. **Verify format identity.** `(:identity-matches-fn format)` over the\n   361\t   requested identity and the root value. For H and R this is a\n   362\t   different hash under a different preimage from step 2 and catches a\n   363\t   stale or swapped index entry, a descriptor disagreement, or a\n   364\t   contract version disagreement (all `:hash-mismatch`, as in B6). For\n   365\t   the storage-derived formats it is `segment-matches?` under the\n   366\t   identity's own algorithm; it still runs, because it is the only check\n   367\t   that the *index* did not point the identity at a different, correctly\n   368\t   stored payload.\n   369\t4. **Validate structural and liveness invariants.** The format's\n   370\t   validator runs over the complete value: for a tree, over the\n   371\t   assembled row set (`:id-resolves`, `:acyclic`, `:root-reachable` are\n   372\t   whole-tree rules that step 2's row-local check cannot run); for a\n   373\t   vector, over the vector; for a register image, including the\n   374\t   ascending, bounded, exact live-set rules. A validator that throws is\n   375\t   `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:validator-refused`.\n   376\t5. **Verify dependency closure.** Two halves.\n   377\t   - *5a, at the linker: obligations.* Two scans run over the verified\n   378\t     value, and the second is subtracted from the first.\n   379\t     `:obligations-fn` yields the free names. `:definitions-fn` yields\n   380\t     the **definition set**: every store key the image itself binds at\n   381\t     module level, which is the section 7.7 store-key query of\n   382\t     `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` (`:vm/store-put` rows, `:store-put`\n   383\t     operands, `yin/def` applications with a constant key) restricted to\n   384\t     constant keys. A module that reads `x` after `(def x 1)` therefore\n   385\t     owes nothing for `x`: the name is bound in the module's own\n   386\t     obligation environment, and it is never flagged. Each remaining\n   387\t     free name is joined with the manifest that delivered the image\n   388\t     (section 8.1): a name under `:yin.module/primitives` becomes\n   389\t     `{:name n :kind :primitive :profile addr}`; a name exported by a\n   390\t     module under `:yin.module/requires` becomes\n   391\t     `{:name n :kind :module :module m :manifest addr}`. A free name\n   392\t     the manifest declares nowhere is `:undeclared-free`; the publisher\n   393\t     did not say what the name means, so no receiver can bind it\n   394\t     identically. The definition set also gives an early export check:\n   395\t     an export under `:yin.module/exports` that is not in the definition\n   396\t     set is `:export-missing` here, before any child runs; the runtime\n   397\t     check of section 7.3 remains for definitions the static scan cannot\n   398\t     see (a key computed at run time). An image requested by bare\n   399\t     identity with no manifest has no declarations; it verifies only if\n   400\t     it has no free names outside its definition set, which is B6's\n   401\t     closed-image case and remains supported.\n   402\t   - *5b, at the receiver: discharge.* Obligations travel with the\n   403\t     verified image in the response. The receiver checks each against\n   404\t     its live state as the first act of installation, before any load:\n   405\t     a `:primitive` obligation is discharged only by a primitive of\n   406\t     equal profile address; a `:module` obligation only by a linked\n   407\t     module of equal manifest address; a name bound in the receiver's\n   408\t     free env or store is `:shadowed-free`; anything else is\n   409\t     `:unresolved-free` naming the obligation and what was found. This\n   410\t     is UCF section 7.5.2's rule (\"checked by profile, not by presence\")\n   411\t     at the linker's grain, and D11's refusal for an image the receiver\n   412\t     cannot bind identically.\n   413\t   Discharge is at the receiver because the receiver's store and free\n   414\t   env are live state; a snapshot sent on the wire is stale by\n   415\t   construction and would license a binding that no longer holds. The\n   416\t   host-policy `fetch` (section 6.4), which runs in one process with the\n   417\t   receiver in hand, runs both halves before returning.\n   418\t6. **Return the verified image.** `{:status :ok :format f :identity i\n   419\t   :address a :value v :obligations [...]}` plus `:parts {address value}`\n   420\t   for a multi-part format and `:derivation {...}` where a manifest\n   421\t   supplied one (section 8.1). Nothing partially verified is ever\n   422\t   returned.\n   423\t\n   424\t### 4.3 Refusal vocabulary\n   425\t\n   426\tEvery refusal is `{:status :refused :reason r}` merged with the step's own\n   427\tevidence, exactly as `yin.vm.linker/refused` builds it.\n   428\t\n   429\t| Reason                  | Step   | Meaning                                  |\n   430\t|-------------------------|--------|------------------------------------------|\n   431\t| `:invalid-request`      | 0      | a request outside the closed key set of  |\n   432\t|                         |        | section 6.3, or with a non-portable value|\n   433\t| `:absent`               | 1 or 2 | no index entry, or no payload at the     |\n   434\t|                         |        | address (root or any part)               |\n   435\t| `:address-mismatch`     | 2      | payload does not hash to its address     |\n   436\t| `:parts-limit`          | 2      | a composition bound on parts, depth, or  |\n   437\t|                         |        | bytes was exceeded                       |\n   438\t| `:hash-mismatch`        | 3      | root value does not match the identity   |\n   439\t| `:descriptor-defect`    | 2 or 4 | row-local or whole-value validation      |\n   440\t|                         |        | failed                                   |\n   441\t| `:contract-mismatch`    | 0      | request or manifest names a contract the |\n   442\t|                         |        | format record does not implement         |\n   443\t| `:undeclared-free`      | 5a     | a free name has no declaration in the    |\n   444\t|                         |        | manifest that delivered the image        |\n   445\t| `:unresolved-free`      | 5b     | an obligation is not discharged by an    |\n   446\t|                         |        | equal profile or manifest                |\n   447\t| `:shadowed-free`        | 5b     | an obligation's name is bound by the     |\n   448\t|                         |        | receiver's free env or store             |\n   449\t| `:unsupported-format`   | 0      | the receiver holds no kernel or format   |\n   450\t|                         |        | record for the requested format          |\n   451\t| `:module-name-mismatch` | 8.1    | the manifest declares a name other than  |\n   452\t|                         |        | the one it was resolved under            |\n   453\t| `:ambiguous-name`       | 8.2    | more than one accepted assertion for a   |\n   454\t|                         |        | name at the snapshot                     |\n   455\t| `:derivation-mismatch`  | 8.1    | an image's derivation record does not    |\n   456\t|                         |        | lead from the manifest's tree, or a      |\n   457\t|                         |        | verifying re-lowering disagrees          |\n   458\t| `:unverified-derivation`| 8.1    | a verifying link cannot recompute the    |\n   459\t|                         |        | derivation (profile not implemented, or  |\n   460\t|                         |        | tree unavailable) and refuses to trust   |\n   461\t| `:unauthenticated`      | 8.2    | an assertion carries no proof the        |\n   462\t|                         |        | composition's verifier accepts           |\n   463\t| `:export-missing`       | 7.3    | the evaluated module did not bind an     |\n   464\t|                         |        | export the manifest names                |\n   465\t| `:require-cycle`        | 7.4    | a child install requires a module that   |\n   466\t|                         |        | is itself installing in its ancestry     |\n   467\t| `:pairing-mismatch`     | verify | B6's same-root check (now a case of      |\n   468\t|                         |        | `:derivation-mismatch`, kept by name)    |\n   469\t\n   470\t`:unsupported-format` is the linker's instance of the host-boundary rule\n   471\tthat a host with no implementation for an effect emits a qualified\n   472\tunsupported result, \"a correct outcome, not a gap to be filled\"\n   473\t(`datom.world.md`). It lets a receiver decline an R request and, where\n   474\tthe composition permits, fall back to H by the manifest's derivations.\n   475\t\n   476\tA stepped link additionally reports `:pending` (section 6.3), which is\n   477\tnot a refusal: it is the \"not yet\" of a non-blocking read.\n   478\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
