{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '479,595p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 479\"","aggregated_output":"   479\t## 5. Format records for the four backends\n   480\t\n   481\tThree records bind existing code; the AST record's free-name scanner is\n   482\tthe section 4.5 query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`, implemented as\n   483\t`yin.vm/free-names`.\n   484\t\n   485\t### 5.1 `:yin.ast/code` (the AST walker)\n   486\t\n   487\t```clojure\n   488\t{:format              :yin.ast/code\n   489\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   490\t :identity-fn         (fn [body] (jing/segment-key body))\n   491\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [root-id body] (jing/segment-matches? root-id\n   492\t                                                                  body))\n   493\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [body] (row-local-defect body))\n   494\t :validate-fn         (fn [tree] (yin.vm/validate-rows tree))\n   495\t :obligations-fn      (fn [tree] (yin.vm/free-names (relation tree)\n   496\t                                                    (occurrences tree)\n   497\t                                                    (:root tree)))\n   498\t :definitions-fn      (fn [tree] (store-put-keys (relation tree)))\n   499\t :parts-fn            (fn [body] (body-child-ids body))}\n   500\t```\n   501\t\n   502\tPayload: one row body `[tag & slots]` per address, exactly as\n   503\t`yin.vm.content/materialize-tree!` stores it (D3: individual rows, no pack\n   504\tformat; the body is what is hashed, and the id is derived from it). The\n   505\tidentity is the root row's id. Steps 2 and 3 therefore hash the fetched\n   506\tbody as received; the address is prepended only when the linker assembles\n   507\t`{id [id tag & slots]}` for step 4, the shape `validate-rows` takes.\n   508\t`row-local-defect` runs the `:tag`, `:arity`, `:slot-kind`, and\n   509\t`:saturation` rules of section 7.4 over one body, so a malformed row\n   510\tnever has its slots followed. Step 2's worklist follows `node` and\n   511\t`nodes` slots by the grammar's positions, the walk\n   512\t`yin.vm.content/load-rows` performs today; that function's throwing\n   513\tsurface is retired in favor of the linker's refusals (section 9).\n   514\tFree names are the conservative, occurrence-scoped set. Loading is\n   515\t`yin.vm.ast-walker/vm-load-rows`.\n   516\t\n   517\t### 5.2 `:yin.semantic/code` (the semantic VM)\n   518\t\n   519\t```clojure\n   520\t{:format              :yin.semantic/code\n   521\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   522\t :identity-fn         jing/segment-key\n   523\t :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?\n   524\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   525\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   526\t :obligations-fn      semantic-free-names\n   527\t :definitions-fn      semantic-definitions\n   528\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   529\t```\n   530\t\n   531\tPayload: the canonical positional instruction tuple vector (UCF section\n   532\t7.3.2), stored as the exact vector at its own `segment-key`; nothing\n   533\telse may hash there (UCF section 7.3.4). The identity is that address.\n   534\t`well-formed-vector?` is the section 7.5 grammar. `semantic-free-names`\n   535\tscans `:var` operands not bound by an enclosing closure's params, the\n   536\t`$code` query of section 7.7; the linker module defines it, as B6\n   537\tdefined the two de Bruijn scanners. The contract stamp is UCF's\n   538\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v2\"}`; a link request for this format carries the\n   539\tstamp, and the receiver's index is keyed per stamp (UCF section 7.3.3).\n   540\tLoading is `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`, which writes the address to the\n   541\timage and the alias column.\n   542\t\n   543\t### 5.3 `:yin.debruijn.code` (the stack VM)\n   544\t\n   545\t```clojure\n   546\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code\n   547\t :contract            \"b1\"\n   548\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash\n   549\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash v)))\n   550\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   551\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   552\t :obligations-fn      stack-free-names\n   553\t :definitions-fn      stack-definitions\n   554\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   555\t```\n   556\t\n   557\tUnchanged from B6 section 5.1 in substance. The identity H is\n   558\t`image-hash` over the descriptor hash (which embeds the lowering contract\n   559\tversion) and the canonical vector; the `=` here compares two values of\n   560\tone contract-pinned hash and is not a Class 3 site. Free names are\n   561\t`:load-free` operands. Loading is `yin.vm.debruijn.stack/load-image`;\n   562\t`yin.repl`'s `append-stack-image` shows the relocation a second image\n   563\tneeds beside a held one.\n   564\t\n   565\t### 5.4 `:yin.debruijn.register` (the register VM)\n   566\t\n   567\t```clojure\n   568\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.register\n   569\t :contract            \"r1\"\n   570\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash\n   571\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [R v]\n   572\t                        (= R (yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash\n   573\t                               v)))\n   574\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect\n   575\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect\n   576\t :obligations-fn      register-free-names\n   577\t :definitions-fn      register-definitions\n   578\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   579\t```\n   580\t\n   581\tUnchanged from B6 section 5.2 in substance. Validation includes the\n   582\tlive-set rules; free names are `[:load-free rd name]` operands across all\n   583\tbodies. Loading is `yin.vm.debruijn.register/load-image`.\n   584\t\n   585\t### 5.5 Same-root pairing becomes derivation verification\n   586\t\n   587\tB6 section 7 paired H and R by mint-time datoms and verified the pair by\n   588\tre-lowering. With four formats the pair generalizes to the manifest's\n   589\tderivation records (section 8.1): one canonical tree, and one\n   590\tcontent-addressed record per format leading from that tree to the\n   591\tformat's identity. `trusted-fallback` and `verifying-fallback` keep their\n   592\tB6 names and shapes and read the derivation from the manifest; the\n   593\t`:pairing-mismatch` reason is retained as the name of a\n   594\t`:derivation-mismatch` raised during a fallback.\n   595\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
