{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1184,1251p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 1184\"","aggregated_output":"  1184\t### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\n  1185\t\n  1186\tThe namespace keeps its shape and changes its contents.\n  1187\t\n  1188\t| Today                        | After                                       |\n  1189\t|------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|\n  1190\t| `register-module r name fns` | `register-host-module r name fns profiles`  |\n  1191\t|                              | (rules below); no code fetched, because the |\n  1192\t|                              | host is the boundary                        |\n  1193\t| `resolve-module r sym`       | unchanged signature; reads `:bindings`      |\n  1194\t| `require-handler`            | registry hit answers; installing joins the  |\n  1195\t|                              | waiter set; miss mints, parks, and emits    |\n  1196\t|                              | (section 7.2); never throws for absence     |\n  1197\t| `register-effect-handler`    | unchanged                                   |\n  1198\t| `stream-module`              | a host module; `register-stream-module`     |\n  1199\t|                              | calls `register-host-module`                |\n  1200\t| `default-registry`           | unchanged                                   |\n  1201\t| (new) `link-module r m d s`  | the `linked` transition of section 7.3      |\n  1202\t\n  1203\t**`register-host-module` enforces UCF profile classes.** Every binding\n  1204\tmust carry a profile in the shape of `yin.vm/primitive-profiles`, and\n  1205\tregistration refuses (throws, as a host assembly defect detected before\n  1206\tany operation runs) unless the profile's class is `:pure`, or\n  1207\t`:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, and\n  1208\t`:yin.k/host-state` is `:none`. A `:host`-class function, a function\n  1209\twith undeclared host state, or a binding with no profile is refused. An\n  1210\t`:effectful` export must return plain effect data for the engine to\n  1211\tinterpret; it may not perform IO. `stream/make` is exactly such a pure\n  1212\teffect constructor, and the engine's `:make-stream` capability remains\n  1213\tthe explicit boundary that performs the creation. A host module is\n  1214\tentered as an already-linked manifest with `:yin.module/tree` absent,\n  1215\t`:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its exports listed under\n  1216\t`:yin.module/primitives` by profile address.\n  1217\t\n  1218\t**The host module is the trusted composition boundary, and the check\n  1219\tabove is a declaration check, not a proof.** A host function is opaque\n  1220\thost code: nothing the linker or the engine can inspect proves that a\n  1221\tfunction declared `:pure` performs no IO or holds no state. The profile\n  1222\tis a warranty the composition gives, in the same sense UCF section 7.5.2\n  1223\tcalls a `:host-state :none` claim \"a publication's warranty\". The\n  1224\tobligations therefore fall where they can be met:\n  1225\t\n  1226\t- *The composition* is responsible for every host module it registers:\n  1227\t  the function behaves as its profile declares, is reviewed and tested\n  1228\t  as trusted code, and is published with its profile record so a\n  1229\t  receiver can check equality. Registering a host module extends the\n  1230\t  trusted computing base of every VM that composition wires, and a\n  1231\t  composition should register the fewest it can.\n  1232\t- *The linker* verifies what is verifiable: profile shape and class at\n  1233\t  registration, profile-address equality at discharge (step 5b), and\n  1234\t  that no host function ever arrives by linking. It makes no claim\n  1235\t  beyond those.\n  1236\t- *Runtime confinement*, where a composition needs it, is not a linker\n  1237\t  mechanism. It is the capability discipline of\n  1238\t  `docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`: an effectful host function\n  1239\t  receives the resources it may touch as explicit capability tokens in\n  1240\t  its effect's interpretation, and a token it was not handed it cannot\n  1241\t  use. That discipline belongs to the engine's effect handlers and the\n  1242\t  composition's wiring, and it is the only way a `:pure` or\n  1243\t  `:effectful` declaration becomes enforceable at run time. Until a\n  1244\t  composition wires it, a host module's declaration is trusted, and this\n  1245\t  document says so rather than implying a sandbox it does not provide.\n  1246\t\n  1247\tThe registry value's `:modules` map changes from `{name {sym fn}}` to\n  1248\t`{name {:manifest m :address a :derivation d :bindings {sym value}}}`.\n  1249\tNo shim keeps the old entry shape: this is a dev-only repository with no\n  1250\tdeployed registries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1251\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
