{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1025,1183p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 1025\"","aggregated_output":"  1025\t## 8. The manifest registry\n  1026\t\n  1027\t### 8.1 The module manifest\n  1028\t\n  1029\tA manifest is content: one map, materialized in `dao.jing`, named by its\n  1030\taddress. It replaces the `{sym fn}` dictionary entry.\n  1031\t\n  1032\t```clojure\n  1033\t{:yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1034\t :yin.module/contract    \"v2\"\n  1035\t :yin.module/tree        :segment/...        ; the one canonical tree\n  1036\t :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code     :segment/...  ; record\n  1037\t                          :yin.debruijn.code     :segment/...  ; record\n  1038\t                          :yin.debruijn.register :segment/...} ; record\n  1039\t :yin.module/index       {H :segment/... R :segment/...}       ; optional\n  1040\t :yin.module/exports     #{'foo 'bar}\n  1041\t :yin.module/requires    {'other.lib :segment/...}             ; manifest\n  1042\t :yin.module/primitives  {'println :yin.k.pp/sha256-...}       ; profile\n  1043\t :yin.module/footprint   {:store-keys #{} :effects #{}}}       ; UCF 7.6.1\n  1044\t```\n  1045\t\n  1046\tRules:\n  1047\t\n  1048\t- **One tree.** `:yin.module/tree` is the root row id of the canonical\n  1049\t  AST the module was authored as. The `:yin.ast/code` image *is* this\n  1050\t  tree, so it has no derivation record.\n  1051\t- **One derivation record per lowered format.** Each value under\n  1052\t  `:yin.module/derivations` is the address of a content-addressed\n  1053\t  derivation record in the shape `yin.vm.ledger/derive-record` mints:\n  1054\t  `{:yin.ledger/op :derive :yin.ledger/input tree\n  1055\t  :yin.ledger/output identity :yin.ledger/function f\n  1056\t  :yin.ledger/profile {...}}`. The linker fetches the record (through a\n  1057\t  `:yin.ledger/record` format record: `segment-matches?` identity, a\n  1058\t  validator over these keys, no parts, no obligations) and checks\n  1059\t  `:yin.ledger/input` equals `:yin.module/tree` and `:yin.ledger/output`\n  1060\t  is the identity it then fetches. A record leading from a different\n  1061\t  tree, or to a different identity, is `:derivation-mismatch`. Four\n  1062\t  individually valid images from four different trees therefore cannot\n  1063\t  share a manifest, and a swapped image fails before load.\n  1064\t- **Contract before content.** Immediately after the manifest passes\n  1065\t  steps 2 to 4, `:yin.module/contract` is checked against the format\n  1066\t  record for the requested format (`:contract-mismatch`), before the\n  1067\t  name check and before any derivation or image is fetched (section\n  1068\t  4.2, step 0).\n  1069\t- **Verifying and trusting are two policies, and verifying never\n  1070\t  trusts.** The linker's `:derivation` policy is one of `:verifying` or\n  1071\t  `:trusted`, chosen by the composition; there is no policy under which\n  1072\t  a verifying link accepts a claim it did not recompute.\n  1073\t  - Under `:verifying`, for every image it delivers the linker fetches\n  1074\t    the manifest's tree through the `:yin.ast/code` record (steps 2 to\n  1075\t    4, so the tree itself is verified), re-lowers it under the exact\n  1076\t    per-format profile the derivation record names (`\"ast-to-bytecode\"`\n  1077\t    for `:yin.semantic/code`, the B2 stack lowering for\n  1078\t    `:yin.debruijn.code`, the R1 register lowering for\n  1079\t    `:yin.debruijn.register`, each pinned by its own\n  1080\t    `:yin.ledger/profile` map), and compares the recomputed identity to\n  1081\t    `:yin.ledger/output` (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section 5.2.2, step\n  1082\t    2). Inequality is `:derivation-mismatch`. If the linker does not\n  1083\t    implement that exact profile, or the tree is `:absent`, or the tree\n  1084\t    fails its own verification, the link is refused\n  1085\t    `:unverified-derivation` naming the profile and what was missing.\n  1086\t    It is never downgraded to trust.\n  1087\t  - Under `:trusted`, the linker checks only the record's input and\n  1088\t    output addresses (the rule above) and reports `:trust :composition`\n  1089\t    in the outcome, exactly as B6's trusted fallback did and never\n  1090\t    silently. A composition that chooses `:trusted` has chosen to\n  1091\t    accept the publisher's lowering, and the outcome says so.\n  1092\t  The B6 fallback pair maps onto these: `verifying-fallback` is the\n  1093\t  `:verifying` policy applied to an H image selected in place of an\n  1094\t  unsupported R; `trusted-fallback` is `:trusted` applied the same way.\n  1095\t  The `:yin.ast/code` image needs no derivation under either policy: it\n  1096\t  is the tree, verified by content.\n  1097\t- **The name is verified.** Immediately after the manifest passes steps\n  1098\t  2 to 4, the linker compares `:yin.module/name` with the\n  1099\t  `:yin.link/name` it was resolved under; inequality is\n  1100\t  `:module-name-mismatch` naming both. A name-environment entry can\n  1101\t  therefore point only at a manifest that claims that name.\n  1102\t- `:yin.module/index` maps contract-pinned identities to their storage\n  1103\t  addresses, the H and R indexes of B6 section 6 carried beside the\n  1104\t  identities they resolve. It is merged into linker-local `:indexes`\n  1105\t  when the manifest is verified, never consulted from the wire.\n  1106\t- `:yin.module/exports` are names, checked after the child evaluation\n  1107\t  (section 7.3). `:yin.module/requires` maps each required module to the\n  1108\t  manifest address the publisher linked against; `:yin.module/primitives`\n  1109\t  maps each assumed host function to its profile address (UCF section\n  1110\t  7.5.2). Together they are the declarations step 5a joins free names\n  1111\t  with.\n  1112\t- `:yin.module/footprint` is what `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md`\n  1113\t  needs to report `:complete`; an undeclared footprint is `:incomplete`,\n  1114\t  never a silent under-approximation.\n  1115\t- The manifest is verified like any content: a `:yin.module/manifest`\n  1116\t  format record with `:identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?`, a\n  1117\t  validator over the keys above, no parts, no obligations.\n  1118\t\n  1119\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n  1120\t\n  1121\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\n  1122\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\n  1123\t\n  1124\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\n  1125\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\n  1126\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\n  1127\t\n  1128\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\n  1129\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\n  1130\timplemented and tested.\n  1131\t\n  1132\t- An assertion is the datoms `[name :yin.module/manifest address]`,\n  1133\t  `[name :yin.module/asserted-by principal]`, and a **proof**,\n  1134\t  transacted together. A bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone\n  1135\t  can write and is never honored on its own; an assertion whose proof\n  1136\t  is absent or fails verification is `:unauthenticated` and discarded\n  1137\t  before counting. Two proof kinds are admitted, and the composition's\n  1138\t  `:authority` declares, per principal, which one it expects:\n  1139\t  - *Signature.* `[name :yin.module/signature sig]`, where `sig` signs\n  1140\t    the canonical bytes (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) of\n  1141\t    `{:name name :manifest address :asserted-by principal}` under the\n  1142\t    principal's public key. `:authority` holds, per principal, the key\n  1143\t    and a composition-supplied verify function; the linker calls the\n  1144\t    function and implements no cryptographic primitive itself (a host\n  1145\t    library sits behind the function, as `dao.jing` does for hashing).\n  1146\t    The signature is over content, so it survives every carrier and\n  1147\t    can be checked by any host that holds the key.\n  1148\t  - *Attested log.* The assertion stream is a one-writer log\n  1149\t    (`dao.stream.md`, *Concurrency*) whose writer the composition\n  1150\t    authenticated at attachment and bound to one principal; `:authority`\n  1151\t    names the stream's `:dao.stream/identity` beside that principal, and\n  1152\t    every assertion read from that identity, at the snapshot, counts as\n  1153\t    proven by it. The proof here is the composition's attachment\n  1154\t    discipline, and it holds only within the reach of that discipline:\n  1155\t    an assertion copied off that log onto another medium carries no\n  1156\t    proof and is `:unauthenticated` there. A composition that needs\n  1157\t    assertions to travel uses signatures.\n  1158\t  A principal declared with neither kind cannot assert anything.\n  1159\t- The linker's `:authority` names the accepted principals with their\n  1160\t  proof kind and material, and the **snapshot**: either a published\n  1161\t  index manifest address (`dao.space.index`) or a cursor position on\n  1162\t  the assertion stream. The linker reads exactly that snapshot;\n  1163\t  assertions appended afterwards do not exist for it until the\n  1164\t  composition advances the snapshot, which is an ordinary `link-state`\n  1165\t  rebuild, never an ambient re-read.\n  1166\t- At the snapshot, for one name: unauthenticated assertions and\n  1167\t  assertions by undeclared principals are discarded; retractions are\n  1168\t  honored only when they carry the same proof as the assertion they\n  1169\t  retract; the distinct manifest addresses remaining are counted.\n  1170\t  Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is `:absent`. More than one is\n  1171\t  `:ambiguous-name` naming every remaining address and asserter, and no\n  1172\t  address is chosen by recency, order, or any other rule.\n  1173\t- Provenance is data the outcome carries: a successful resolution names\n  1174\t  the asserter, the proof kind, and the snapshot under\n  1175\t  `:yin.link/provenance` so a receiver can record which claim it acted\n  1176\t  on.\n  1177\t\n  1178\tAn entry is a claim. The manifest it names is verified, and its name is\n  1179\tverified against the entry (section 8.1). Which principals a composition\n  1180\tdeclares, and how it obtains and rotates their keys, is the composition's\n  1181\t(section 12); what the linker does with a declared principal's assertion\n  1182\tis fixed above.\n  1183\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
