{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1252,1483p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 1252\"","aggregated_output":"  1252\t## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n  1253\t\n  1254\tFive steps, each landing green on all three hosts before the next. The\n  1255\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1256\t\n  1257\t```mermaid\n  1258\tflowchart TD\n  1259\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1260\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1261\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1262\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1263\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1264\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1265\t```\n  1266\t\n  1267\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1268\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1269\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1270\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1271\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1272\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1273\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1274\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1275\t\n  1276\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1277\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1278\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1279\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1280\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1281\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1282\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1283\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1284\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1285\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1286\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1287\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1288\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1289\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1290\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1291\t`:blake3`.\n  1292\t\n  1293\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1294\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1295\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1296\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1297\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1298\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1299\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1300\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1301\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1302\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1303\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1304\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1305\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1306\t\n  1307\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1308\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1309\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1310\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1311\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1312\tundeclared principal is ignored; retraction with matching proof is\n  1313\thonored and without it is ignored; two proven assertions refuse\n  1314\t`:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then: the manifest and derivation\n  1315\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1316\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1317\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1318\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1319\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1320\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1321\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1322\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1323\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1324\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1325\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1326\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1327\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1328\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1329\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1330\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1331\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1332\t`:require-cycle`; `(vm :stack)` and `(vm :register)` in `yin.repl` link\n  1333\tthe same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\n  1334\t\n  1335\t**M5. `yin.repl` wiring.** The REPL composes the link pair per VM and\n  1336\tthe content pair per connection (`connect` already opens the RPC\n  1337\tclient). `(require 'foo)` at the prompt exercises the whole path.\n  1338\t\n  1339\tCoexistence during M4: host modules are entered by\n  1340\t`register-host-module` from the first commit of M4, so every existing\n  1341\tcomposition keeps working while linked modules are added. There is no\n  1342\tperiod in which two registry shapes coexist.\n  1343\t\n  1344\t## 10. File box\n  1345\t\n  1346\t```text\n  1347\tRenamed:  src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc\n  1348\t            -> src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc            (M1)\n  1349\t          test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc\n  1350\t            -> test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc           (M1)\n  1351\tNew:      test/yin/vm/linker_step_test.cljc           (M3)\n  1352\t          test/yin/vm/linker_authority_test.cljc      (M4 entry)\n  1353\t          test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc        (M4)\n  1354\tEdited:   src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc                 (M4)\n  1355\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc  (:link-request, :link-response,\n  1356\t                                        :install wait reasons; the\n  1357\t                                        install child)             (M4)\n  1358\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc (retire load-rows,\n  1359\t                                        fetch-vector)              (M2)\n  1360\t          src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc                      (M5)\n  1361\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n  1362\t            (section 7.4.1 rows, section 7.4.3 variants)           (M4)\n  1363\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n  1364\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n  1365\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names, primitive-profiles)\n  1366\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n  1367\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1368\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1369\tMust not change:\n  1370\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1371\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing, any kernel's step function\n  1372\t```\n  1373\t\n  1374\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `discharge`, `link-state`,\n  1375\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`,\n  1376\t`semantic-format`, `stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`,\n  1377\t`record-format`, the four free-name scanners, the four definition\n  1378\tscanners, `row-local-defect`, `index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`,\n  1379\t`trusted-fallback`, `verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`,\n  1380\t`refusal-reasons`.\n  1381\t\n  1382\t## 11. Completion criteria\n  1383\t\n  1384\tStructure:\n  1385\t\n  1386\t1. One `fetch` and one `step` serve all four formats with no\n  1387\t   format-specific branching; a fifth format is one record.\n  1388\t2. No global loader, registry, callback, or cache; every input is an\n  1389\t   argument or VM-state value; no function or handle ever appears in a\n  1390\t   value on the link or content streams.\n  1391\t3. Tri-host parity (JVM, Node, ClojureDart), 0 kondo errors, clean\n  1392\t   cljstyle.\n  1393\t4. This file and `yin.vm.linker` are pure ASCII with every line at most\n  1394\t   80 columns.\n  1395\t\n  1396\tVerification:\n  1397\t\n  1398\t5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n  1399\t   formats where applicable, through both `fetch` and `step`.\n  1400\t6. A payload whose address is valid but whose identity is not the one\n  1401\t   requested is refused for every format, including the two whose\n  1402\t   identity is a storage address, and under every registered algorithm.\n  1403\t7. A request naming a contract the format record does not implement is\n  1404\t   `:contract-mismatch` before validation runs.\n  1405\t8. A malformed row is refused before any of its children is requested,\n  1406\t   and every composition bound produces `:parts-limit`.\n  1407\t9. Local `fetch` produces exactly the content-pair traffic the stepped\n  1408\t   path produces and holds no content handle.\n  1409\t\n  1410\tRequire:\n  1411\t\n  1412\t10. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\n  1413\t    parks, links, installs through the child phases, and resumes with\n  1414\t    `'foo`; the same over the JVM WebSocket content path.\n  1415\t11. The registry value holds no function that arrived by linking; every\n  1416\t    linked module's `:bindings` came from an isolated child evaluation\n  1417\t    that reached halt with every export bound.\n  1418\t12. UCF section 7.4.1 carries `:link-request`, `:link-response`, and\n  1419\t    `:install` safepoints, section 7.4.3 their pending variants, and a\n  1420\t    parked entry of each kind lifts and lowers through UCF's round-trip\n  1421\t    test.\n  1422\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1423\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name`,\n  1424\t    discards unproven assertions as `:unauthenticated`, and ignores\n  1425\t    undeclared principals, at a fixed snapshot.\n  1426\t15. A module that defines a name and then reads it produces no\n  1427\t    obligation for that name; an export absent from the definition set\n  1428\t    is `:export-missing` before any child runs.\n  1429\t16. Two install children and the root task, each with counter `0`,\n  1430\t    issue three requests on one link pair with three distinct ids, and\n  1431\t    each restores on its own.\n  1432\t17. On every backend, an exported closure applied in the parent after\n  1433\t    `linked` runs the same body it ran in the child; a stack and a\n  1434\t    register closure exported from a child whose image was appended at\n  1435\t    a nonzero offset in the parent resolve to the relocated pc.\n  1436\t18. Under `:derivation :verifying`, a manifest whose record names a\n  1437\t    profile the linker does not implement is `:unverified-derivation`,\n  1438\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  1439\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  1440\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  1441\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  1442\t\n  1443\t## 12. Open decisions\n  1444\t\n  1445\tRecorded so a later plan does not rediscover them. None blocks M1 to M3;\n  1446\tthe first concerns material the composition supplies to a policy section\n  1447\t8.2 fixes.\n  1448\t\n  1449\t- **Key material and rotation.** Section 8.2 fixes the two proof kinds\n  1450\t  and what the linker does with a proven, unproven, or undeclared\n  1451\t  assertion. How a composition obtains a principal's public key, rotates\n  1452\t  it, and revokes it, and which signature scheme the composition-supplied\n  1453\t  verify function implements, are composition decisions. A key-rotation\n  1454\t  event is itself a candidate assertion under the same policy, which a\n  1455\t  later design may take up.\n  1456\t- **Runtime capability confinement of host modules.** Section 8.3 names\n  1457\t  the host module as the trusted composition boundary and the capability\n  1458\t  discipline of `docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md` as the only run-time\n  1459\t  enforcement. Wiring tokens into effect handlers is engine and\n  1460\t  composition work outside this document.\n  1461\t- **SCC identity.** B7 hashes a mutually recursive component as one unit\n  1462\t  with canonical member ordering. Whether that unit is a manifest of\n  1463\t  manifests or a single image per format is undecided; section 7.4\n  1464\t  fixes only the response shape and the cycle refusal.\n  1465\t- **Failure policy.** Retry, deadline, and permanent absence for a\n  1466\t  `:pending` link are the composition's (D6). Whether `yin.repl` adopts\n  1467\t  the `dao.jing.remote` timing options or its own is an M5 decision.\n  1468\t- **Contract-pinned AST and semantic identities.** Strict decoupling of\n  1469\t  storage address from VM identity holds for H and R only (section 3).\n  1470\t  Pinning `:yin.ast/code` and `:yin.semantic/code` identities to a\n  1471\t  contract hash, with explicit identity-to-address indexes, is an\n  1472\t  amendment to UCF section 7.3.2 and `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section\n  1473\t  4.1. The linker is prepared for it: `:identity-matches-fn` and\n  1474\t  `:indexes` are the only slots that would change.\n  1475\t- **A stepped DHT client.** The DHT is served behind the content\n  1476\t  boundary (section 6.1). A portable, non-blocking DHT client that could\n  1477\t  sit on the linker's side is a `dao.jing.dht` design.\n  1478\t- **Unrecognized outcomes.** `dao.stream.md` OD-1 proposes that a\n  1479\t  consumer treat an unrecognized outcome as refused and not retryable.\n  1480\t  The stepped core follows that rule once OD-1 is accepted; until then\n  1481\t  it classifies unknown content-server answers as `transport-error`, as\n  1482\t  `dao.stream.observe/step` does.\n  1483\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
