{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '675,735p;1205,1250p;1250,1345p'\"","aggregated_output":"   675\t```clojure\n   676\t(link-state opts)               ; -> state; no socket, atom, or scheduler\n   677\t(request-link state request)    ; -> [state link-id]\n   678\t(step state budget)             ; -> {:state s :completions [...]\n   679\t                                ;     :diagnostics [...]}\n   680\t(abandon state link-id reason)  ; -> state\n   681\t```\n   682\t\n   683\tA `request` is plain data and nothing else. Its closed key set is\n   684\t`:yin.link/id`, `:yin.link/format`, `:yin.link/contract` (optional), and\n   685\texactly one of `:yin.link/name` or `:yin.link/identity`. The two\n   686\tadmissible shapes:\n   687\t\n   688\t```clojure\n   689\t;; by module name: the linker resolves the manifest (section 8)\n   690\t{:yin.link/id       [:t0 7]                  ; section 7.2, step 3\n   691\t :yin.link/format   :yin.debruijn.code\n   692\t :yin.link/contract \"b1\"\n   693\t :yin.link/name     'my.lib}\n   694\t\n   695\t;; by bare identity: B6's closed-image path, no manifest\n   696\t{:yin.link/id       [:t0 8]\n   697\t :yin.link/format   :yin.debruijn.code\n   698\t :yin.link/contract \"b1\"\n   699\t :yin.link/identity H}\n   700\t```\n   701\t\n   702\tA request carrying both `:yin.link/name` and `:yin.link/identity`, or\n   703\tneither, is `:invalid-request`, as is any key outside the set or any\n   704\tvalue that is not a scalar, keyword, symbol, address, or the id vector.\n   705\tA request carries no index, no receiver, no function, and no handle. The\n   706\trefusal is appended on the response stream under the request's id where\n   707\tthe id is well formed, and under `:yin.link/id nil` otherwise; it is\n   708\tnever processed further. The receiver's capabilities do not travel\n   709\tbecause discharge happens at the receiver (section 4.2, 5b).\n   710\t\n   711\t`step` advances every in-flight link in a fixed order: re-attempt\n   712\tunsent content requests, poll the content response medium at most\n   713\t`budget` elements, route each correlated response to its link, run the\n   714\tverification step that response enables, issue the next content request\n   715\tthe worklist needs (a part, under `:parts-fn`), and take completions.\n   716\tEach link is a small state machine over the six steps; steps 3 to 5a\n   717\tnever touch a stream and run the moment step 2 completes.\n   718\t\n   719\tA completion is the step-6 result or a refusal, tagged with its link id:\n   720\t\n   721\t```clojure\n   722\t{:yin.link/id 7 :status :ok :manifest m :derivation d :image {...}}\n   723\t{:yin.link/id 7 :status :refused :reason :absent :address a}\n   724\t```\n   725\t\n   726\tA link with no completion yet is `:pending`; the caller steps again\n   727\twhen it chooses. Retry cadence, deadlines, and permanent-absence policy\n   728\tare the composition's, as D6 states: streams report, they do not decide.\n   729\t\n   730\t`abandon` retires a link's bookkeeping and completes it `:lost` with the\n   731\tgiven reason, so a caller that gives up still receives exactly one\n   732\tcompletion and never reuses the id.\n   733\t\n   734\t### 6.4 `fetch` is host policy over an explicit runtime\n   735\t\n  1205\tregistration refuses (throws, as a host assembly defect detected before\n  1206\tany operation runs) unless the profile's class is `:pure`, or\n  1207\t`:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, and\n  1208\t`:yin.k/host-state` is `:none`. A `:host`-class function, a function\n  1209\twith undeclared host state, or a binding with no profile is refused. An\n  1210\t`:effectful` export must return plain effect data for the engine to\n  1211\tinterpret; it may not perform IO. `stream/make` is exactly such a pure\n  1212\teffect constructor, and the engine's `:make-stream` capability remains\n  1213\tthe explicit boundary that performs the creation. A host module is\n  1214\tentered as an already-linked manifest with `:yin.module/tree` absent,\n  1215\t`:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its exports listed under\n  1216\t`:yin.module/primitives` by profile address.\n  1217\t\n  1218\t**The host module is the trusted composition boundary, and the check\n  1219\tabove is a declaration check, not a proof.** A host function is opaque\n  1220\thost code: nothing the linker or the engine can inspect proves that a\n  1221\tfunction declared `:pure` performs no IO or holds no state. The profile\n  1222\tis a warranty the composition gives, in the same sense UCF section 7.5.2\n  1223\tcalls a `:host-state :none` claim \"a publication's warranty\". The\n  1224\tobligations therefore fall where they can be met:\n  1225\t\n  1226\t- *The composition* is responsible for every host module it registers:\n  1227\t  the function behaves as its profile declares, is reviewed and tested\n  1228\t  as trusted code, and is published with its profile record so a\n  1229\t  receiver can check equality. Registering a host module extends the\n  1230\t  trusted computing base of every VM that composition wires, and a\n  1231\t  composition should register the fewest it can.\n  1232\t- *The linker* verifies what is verifiable: profile shape and class at\n  1233\t  registration, profile-address equality at discharge (step 5b), and\n  1234\t  that no host function ever arrives by linking. It makes no claim\n  1235\t  beyond those.\n  1236\t- *Runtime confinement*, where a composition needs it, is not a linker\n  1237\t  mechanism. It is the capability discipline of\n  1238\t  `docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`: an effectful host function\n  1239\t  receives the resources it may touch as explicit capability tokens in\n  1240\t  its effect's interpretation, and a token it was not handed it cannot\n  1241\t  use. That discipline belongs to the engine's effect handlers and the\n  1242\t  composition's wiring, and it is the only way a `:pure` or\n  1243\t  `:effectful` declaration becomes enforceable at run time. Until a\n  1244\t  composition wires it, a host module's declaration is trusted, and this\n  1245\t  document says so rather than implying a sandbox it does not provide.\n  1246\t\n  1247\tThe registry value's `:modules` map changes from `{name {sym fn}}` to\n  1248\t`{name {:manifest m :address a :derivation d :bindings {sym value}}}`.\n  1249\tNo shim keeps the old entry shape: this is a dev-only repository with no\n  1250\tdeployed registries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1250\tdeployed registries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1251\t\n  1252\t## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n  1253\t\n  1254\tFive steps, each landing green on all three hosts before the next. The\n  1255\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1256\t\n  1257\t```mermaid\n  1258\tflowchart TD\n  1259\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1260\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1261\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1262\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1263\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1264\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1265\t```\n  1266\t\n  1267\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1268\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1269\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1270\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1271\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1272\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1273\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1274\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1275\t\n  1276\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1277\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1278\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1279\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1280\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1281\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1282\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1283\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1284\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1285\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1286\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1287\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1288\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1289\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1290\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1291\t`:blake3`.\n  1292\t\n  1293\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1294\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1295\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1296\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1297\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1298\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1299\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1300\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1301\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1302\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1303\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1304\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1305\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1306\t\n  1307\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1308\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1309\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1310\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1311\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1312\tundeclared principal is ignored; retraction with matching proof is\n  1313\thonored and without it is ignored; two proven assertions refuse\n  1314\t`:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then: the manifest and derivation\n  1315\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1316\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1317\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1318\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1319\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1320\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1321\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1322\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1323\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1324\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1325\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1326\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1327\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1328\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1329\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1330\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1331\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1332\t`:require-cycle`; `(vm :stack)` and `(vm :register)` in `yin.repl` link\n  1333\tthe same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\n  1334\t\n  1335\t**M5. `yin.repl` wiring.** The REPL composes the link pair per VM and\n  1336\tthe content pair per connection (`connect` already opens the RPC\n  1337\tclient). `(require 'foo)` at the prompt exercises the whole path.\n  1338\t\n  1339\tCoexistence during M4: host modules are entered by\n  1340\t`register-host-module` from the first commit of M4, so every existing\n  1341\tcomposition keeps working while linked modules are added. There is no\n  1342\tperiod in which two registry shapes coexist.\n  1343\t\n  1344\t## 10. File box\n  1345\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
